<ui:UXML xmlns:ui="UnityEngine.UIElements" xmlns:uie="UnityEditor.UIElements" editor-extension-mode="False">
    <!-- Cluck Wars — character select STEP 2 "Build Your Loadout" (2026-09 rework).

         This used to be the WHOLE character-select screen (class pick + passive
         fork + stat preview + two ability pick rows + detail strip + toggles +
         ready button). Class + specialization moved to the new Assets/UI/
         CharacterSelectClass.uxml ("Step 1"); this screen is now ability slots
         only, which is also the actual fix for the historical overlap bug (see
         the CommonScroll/ClassScroll comment below) — the three-column layout
         that used to squeeze this content into ~936px is gone, so the pick rows
         get the full page width.

         Root name CharacterSelectPage is UNCHANGED so any other reference to it
         (scene wiring, MenuUiController's serialized field, which keeps the old
         name "_characterSelectUxml" precisely so the scene reference didn't need
         re-pointing) keeps working.

         Binding contract (MenuUiController.BuildLoadout/RefreshLoadout/
         RefreshSlotBoxes — read those before renaming anything here):
           - BackBtn                                    (goes to Step 1, keeps picks)
           - SlotBox0 / SlotBox1 / SlotBox2 / SlotBox3   (exactly 4, one per
             active-ability slot — v0.7 made this uniform across all classes)
           - CommonCards, ClassCards                     (unchanged names — the
             containers RebuildPickRows/FillRow populate; only their wrapper
             changed, from a wrapping flex grid to a horizontal ScrollView)
           - CommonHint, CommonCount, ClassHint, ClassCount   (unchanged)
           - AbilityDetail, AbilityDetailName, AbilityDetailText   (unchanged)
           - RangeGuidesToggle, DeveloperModeToggle       (unchanged — kept even
             though the task brief for this screen didn't call them out, because
             MenuUiController.BuildLoadout still binds both; dropping them would
             silently remove the only route to the Ability Lab and the range-
             guide preference from the UI, which nobody asked for)
           - ReadyBtn                                     (unchanged)

         SlotBoxN is deliberately EMPTY markup — RefreshSlotBoxes() does
         box.Clear() and rebuilds its children (icon/sprite, name, numbered
         badge, or the "EMPTY" label) from C# every time, exactly like
         MakeAbilityCard already did for pick-row cards. Anything static placed
         inside a SlotBoxN here would be destroyed the first time the screen is
         shown and never be seen.

         The chicken preview column from the old 3-column layout (art/name/quote)
         is dropped, not shrunk — Step 1 already shows the chicken, and this
         column's actual content (four slots + up to 11 ability cards across two
         rows) needs the width more than a redundant portrait does.

         Sizes follow the MOBILE SIZING CONTRACT at the top of CluckWarsTheme.uss. -->
    <ui:Style src="project://database/Assets/UI/Styles/CluckWarsTheme.uss" />

    <ui:VisualElement name="CharacterSelectPage" class="cw-screen cw-page">

        <!-- Header ribbon (+ back button, absolutely placed top-left). BackBtn
             reuses HomeBtn's visual (.cw-home-btn) but wires to ShowClassSelect,
             not ShowMainMenu — it must not discard the class/specialization/
             ability picks the way leaving via HomeBtn on Step 1 would. -->
        <ui:VisualElement style="align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 12px; flex-shrink: 0;">
            <ui:Button name="BackBtn" text="◀ BACK" class="cw-home-btn" />
            <ui:VisualElement class="cw-ribbon">
                <ui:Label text="BUILD YOUR LOADOUT" class="cw-title" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <ui:VisualElement name="Body" class="cw-cs-detail" style="padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px; padding-bottom: 16px;">

            <!-- Slot boxes — every class now has 4 uniform active-ability slots
                 (v0.7; COMBO used to grant Assassin a 3rd, retired). This row is
                 the slot-arming state machine's only visible control surface:
                 tapping a box arms it (OnSlotBoxTapped), tapping an ability card
                 fills whichever box is armed (OnAbilityCardTapped). Sits above
                 #PickScroll, fixed, so it is never scrolled out of view — the
                 player always has to see which slot the next tap will act on. -->
            <ui:VisualElement name="SlotBoxRow" class="cw-slot-box-row">
                <ui:Button name="SlotBox0" class="cw-slot-box" />
                <ui:Button name="SlotBox1" class="cw-slot-box" />
                <ui:Button name="SlotBox2" class="cw-slot-box" />
                <ui:Button name="SlotBox3" class="cw-slot-box" />
            </ui:VisualElement>

            <!-- The two pick rows live in a ScrollView — same load-bearing
                 `min-height: 0` trick as the old #PickScroll (see
                 .cw-pick-scroll in CluckWarsTheme.uss for why removing it
                 silently un-fixes the scroll). Kept as a vertical safety net
                 around the two rows even though each row no longer wraps
                 internally, in case a future pool/copy change makes the two
                 rows together taller than the column again. -->
            <ui:ScrollView name="PickScroll" mode="Vertical" class="cw-pick-scroll">

                <ui:VisualElement name="CommonRow" class="cw-pick-row cw-well" style="padding: 14px;">
                    <ui:VisualElement class="cw-pick-row__head">
                        <ui:Label text="COMMON" class="cw-pick-row__title" />
                        <ui:Label name="CommonHint" text="optional · any chicken can take these" class="cw-pick-row__hint" />
                        <ui:VisualElement class="cw-pick-row__rule" />
                        <ui:Label name="CommonCount" text="0 EQUIPPED" class="cw-pick-row__count" />
                    </ui:VisualElement>
                    <!-- HORIZONTAL scroll, not a wrapping grid — the actual fix for
                         the documented overlap bug (see .cw-pick-cards below): a
                         row that scrolls sideways has no wrap-collision case
                         regardless of how many cards the pool holds, so Assassin's
                         6-card CLASS pool (vs. 3 for the other three classes) can
                         never again paint over ClassRow/AbilityDetail the way the
                         unscrolled wrapping grid did before ADR 0003, and the way
                         the vertical-wrap version did again after pools widened to
                         8-11 (commit 21ddaa8). #CommonCards/#ClassCards are
                         unchanged names — MenuUiController.FillRow just Clears()
                         and Adds() into whichever VisualElement it finds by that
                         name, so nesting it one level deeper inside a ScrollView
                         is transparent to the controller. -->
                    <ui:ScrollView name="CommonScroll" mode="Horizontal" class="cw-pick-scroll--h">
                        <ui:VisualElement name="CommonCards" class="cw-pick-cards" />
                    </ui:ScrollView>
                </ui:VisualElement>

                <ui:VisualElement name="ClassRow" class="cw-pick-row cw-well" style="padding: 14px;">
                    <ui:VisualElement class="cw-pick-row__head">
                        <ui:Label text="CLASS" class="cw-pick-row__title" />
                        <ui:Label name="ClassHint" text="Warrior only" class="cw-pick-row__hint" />
                        <ui:VisualElement class="cw-pick-row__rule" />
                        <ui:Label name="ClassCount" text="0 EQUIPPED" class="cw-pick-row__count" />
                    </ui:VisualElement>
                    <ui:ScrollView name="ClassScroll" mode="Horizontal" class="cw-pick-scroll--h">
                        <ui:VisualElement name="ClassCards" class="cw-pick-cards" />
                    </ui:ScrollView>
                </ui:VisualElement>

            </ui:ScrollView>

            <!-- Shared ability detail — unchanged semantics/classes from the old
                 single screen (see CluckWarsTheme.uss .cw-ability-detail for why
                 this exists instead of a per-card description). -->
            <ui:VisualElement name="AbilityDetail" class="cw-ability-detail">
                <ui:Label name="AbilityDetailName" text="" class="cw-ability-detail__name" />
                <ui:Label name="AbilityDetailText" text="Tap an ability to see what it does." class="cw-ability-detail__text" />
            </ui:VisualElement>

            <!-- Display options — unchanged from the old single screen (see
                 CluckWarsTheme.uss's "DISPLAY OPTION ROW" block for the full
                 reasoning: no settings screen exists, both toggles live on the
                 screen they are about, and .cw-opt-row is landscape-only). -->
            <ui:VisualElement name="OptionsRow" class="cw-opt-row">
                <ui:Toggle name="RangeGuidesToggle" text="Ability Range Guides" class="cw-opt-toggle" />
                <ui:Label name="RangeGuidesHint" text="Show a faint outline of what each equipped ability can reach." class="cw-opt-hint" />
            </ui:VisualElement>

            <ui:VisualElement name="DevOptionsRow" class="cw-opt-row">
                <ui:Toggle name="DeveloperModeToggle" text="Developer Mode" class="cw-opt-toggle" />
                <ui:Label name="DeveloperModeHint" text="Show the Ability Lab and other developer tools on the main menu." class="cw-opt-hint" />
            </ui:VisualElement>

            <ui:Button name="ReadyBtn" text="PICK ABILITIES" class="cw-btn cw-btn--neutral" style="flex-shrink: 0; letter-spacing: 3px;" />
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <ui:Label name="ConsoleHints" text="←→ Select · A Confirm · LB/RB Tab" class="cw-body cw-console-hints" style="position: absolute; bottom: 12px; left: 24px; opacity: 0.6; display: none;" />
    </ui:VisualElement>
</ui:UXML>
